Subject: Legal Notice regarding interference and partition dispute affecting land purchased through GPA

Sir(s),

Under instructions from and on behalf of my client [Your Name], I hereby issue the following legal notice:

My client purchased the land bearing Survey No. ___, extent ___, situated at ___ village, ___ Mandal, ___ District, through a registered General Power of Attorney (GPA) holder, duly executed by you, the landowner, for valid consideration.

At the time of purchase, the GPA was valid, subsisting, and legally enforceable, and the transaction was completed in good faith after due verification of documents.

Subsequent to the purchase, my client has been facing serious issues and interference from you and your brother, citing internal partition disputes, which were neither disclosed nor pending to the knowledge of my client at the time of sale.

It is submitted that any internal family or partition disputes cannot affect the lawful rights of a bona fide purchaser who has purchased the property through a valid GPA and registered documents.

Your acts of interference, obstruction, and attempts to dispute my client’s lawful possession are illegal, arbitrary, and untenable in the eyes of law.

Therefore, you are hereby called upon to:

Refrain from interfering with my client’s peaceful possession and enjoyment of the said property;

Resolve your internal partition disputes without affecting my client’s rights; and

Confirm in writing that no further claims or obstructions will be raised against my client.

Take notice that if you fail to comply with the above within 15 days from the date of receipt of this notice, my client will be constrained to initiate appropriate civil and criminal proceedings at your risk as to costs and consequences, without any further notice.

This notice is issued without prejudice to all other rights and remedies available to my client under law.

Yours faithfully,
[Advocate Name]
